// CLAIM: a runtime fault names the enclosing function as the user WROTE it — the entry program's
//        internal module prefix never surfaces in a trace.
// GUIDE: SkarnGuide.md (When something goes wrong)
// EXPECT: fail division by zero at line 9 (in boom)
// NOTE: `boom` is reached through a function VALUE on purpose. A direct call to a body this small
//       is INLINED (on by default), and an expanded body has no frame of its own, so the trace
//       would name the call site instead — see fault_inlined_names_call_site.skn, which locks
//       that. An indirect call is never inlined, so this claim still exercises the naming path.
fn boom(n: Int) -> Int { n / 0 }
let f: fn(Int) -> Int = boom
println("${f(3)}")
